-- Q3570: System Availability and Change Management [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Every dependency is a potential failure point requiring recovery planning","Only the primary application needs disaster recovery protection","Dependent systems should be consolidated into one to reduce complexity","Interdependent systems do not materially affect overall recovery time"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Per NIST SP 800-34 Rev. 1, interdependency analysis reveals that each system a business process depends on is a potential single point of failure. The slowest system to recover determines actual process recovery time, so all dependencies must be addressed.
Wrong (B): Planning recovery for only the primary application while ignoring upstream and downstream dependencies creates blind spots that delay actual recovery.
Wrong (C): Consolidating dependent systems introduces greater single-point-of-failure risk rather than reducing complexity in recovery planning.
Wrong (D): Interdependent systems directly affect recovery time because a process cannot resume until all required upstream systems are operational.$EXPL$
