-- Q3580: Security and Control Frameworks [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["To list all employees with access to sensitive organizational data","To record all cybersecurity incidents that occurred in the past year","To document applicable Annex A controls and justify any exclusions","To define the organization''s annual budget for information security"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ISO/IEC 27001:2022 Clause 6.1.3(d), the Statement of Applicability (SoA) is a required document listing all Annex A controls, stating whether each is applicable, and justifying inclusions and exclusions based on the risk assessment.
Wrong (A): An access control matrix documents specific user permissions for operational purposes, not the governance-level control applicability decisions required by ISO 27001.
Wrong (B): An incident log records cybersecurity events for response and analysis, which is separate from the SoA''s purpose of mapping controls to risk assessment findings.
Wrong (D): Security budgeting is a financial planning activity, not a certification requirement addressed by the Statement of Applicability.$EXPL$
