-- Q3599: Security and Control Frameworks [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Monitoring must track both deficiency detection and timely remediation of issues","MTTD is not a recognized metric, so the entire monitoring program is invalid","COSO does not address IT security controls, only financial reporting controls","Monitoring Activities only requires an annual review by external auditors"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Per COSO Internal Control -- Integrated Framework (2013) Principle 16, Monitoring Activities requires tracking both detection of deficiencies and timely remediation to evaluate whether controls are present and functioning. MTTD alone measures detection speed without confirming problems are resolved.
Wrong (B): MTTD is a widely recognized security operations metric; the issue is not the metric itself but the absence of complementary remediation tracking.
Wrong (C): COSO applies to internal controls broadly, including IT security; it is not limited to financial reporting controls within accounting.
Wrong (D): Monitoring Activities requires ongoing internal monitoring built into daily operations, not merely an annual review by external auditors.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3599;

-- Q3600: Security and Control Frameworks [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Both belong under Technological controls as identity verification processes","Both belong under People controls as human-related safeguards","Background check is Physical and visitor badge is Organizational control","Both belong under Organizational controls as governance activities"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ISO 27002:2022 Sections 5-8, People controls (Section 6) cover human-related safeguards. Background checks address personnel screening and visitor badges govern physical access by individuals, both falling under the People theme.
Wrong (A): Technological controls cover IT-related safeguards like encryption and access control systems, not personnel screening or visitor management processes.
Wrong (C): While visitor badges involve physical premises, ISO 27002:2022 classifies both controls under People because they primarily address human behavior and vetting.
Wrong (D): Organizational controls address governance policies and procedures at the enterprise level, not the individual-focused personnel and visitor controls described here.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3600;

-- Q3602: Security and Control Frameworks [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Deploy micro-segmentation across all existing network zones","Replace all legacy firewalls with next-generation models","Require biometric authentication for every user immediately","Identify and classify all assets, data flows, and users first"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Per NIST SP 800-207 Section 2, zero trust implementation begins with comprehensive visibility -- discovering all assets, data flows, and user populations before defining access policies. Without this foundational inventory, meaningful access rules cannot be created.
